$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A schlenk tube equipped with a magnetic stirring bar was charged with
(IMes)AgCl (6.0 μmol), potassium tert-butoxide (1 M solution in THF,
0.018 mmol), an alkyne (0.45 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (0.30 mmol)
and MeOH (1.0 mL). The mixture was stirred at 50 °C for the period as
specified in Table 2 and Scheme 1, and diluted with ethyl acetate before
filtration through a Celite plug. The organic solution was washed twice
with brine and dried over MgSO4. Evaporation of the solvent followed by
silica gecolumm chromatoghy (hexane/dichloromethane as an eluent) or gel
permeation chromatography (chloroform as an eluent) gave the
corresponding product. In 13C NMR spectra, boron-bound carbons were not
detected because of quadrupolar relaxation.
(Z)-4,4,5,5-Tetramethy2-(1-phenylprop-1-en-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (2a)
Isolated in 76% as a pale yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.35 (s, 12H),
1.99 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 3H), 7.24 (s, 1H), 7.24 (tt, J = 7.2, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
7.34 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.39 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H) 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
15.89, 24.83, 83.49, 127.07, 128.00, 129.39, 137.90, 142.34 All the
resonances in 1H and 13C spectra were consistent with reported values.2
