$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Synthesis of
Monoalkyl Potassium Trifluoroborate Salts (19). py•BH3 (0.2 mL, 2 mmol)
was added to a flask containing 5 mL of CH2Cl2 and the reaction was
cooled to 0 °C. Next, I2 (253 mg, 1 mmol) was added in portions. After
gas evolution had ceased, styrene (18a) (0.23 mL, 2mmol) was added and
the reaction was allowed to stir at room temperature for 4 h. The CH2Cl2
was removed and MeOH (3 mL) and KHF2 (4.5M) (5 mL) was added to give a
heterogeneous mixture that was stirred for 30 min. The solution was
diluted with CH3CN (5 mL), solvent was removed (rotatory evaporator), and
the crude product was placed under vacuum (30 minutes). CH3CN (10 mL) was
then added to the crude mixture, the resulting suspension was filtered,
and the filtrate was concentrated (rotatory evaporator). The residue was
then dissolved in acetone (5 mL) and ether (1 mL) was slowly added until
precipitation occurred. The resulting precipitate was isolated via
filtration and dried to provide the desired product 19a, 356 mg (84%),
identical according to NMR comparisons with commercial 19a.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM activation of pyridine borane was done at 1st step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydroboration with Pyridine Borane at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Clay, Julia M.; Vedejs, Edwin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(16), 5766-5767

