$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. Asymmetric Rhodium-Directed
anti-Markovnikov Regioselective Boracyclopentannulation General
Procedure: A 10 mL oven-dried Schlenk flask was charged with the
appropriate NHC-BH3 (0.125 mmol), [Rh(nbd)2]BF4 (2.5 mg, 6.2 μmol, 5
mol%) and (S)-Xylyl-MeO-BIPHEP (3.6 mg, 6.2 μmol, 5 mol%) under argon.
Then, dry degassed dichloromethane (1 mL) was added and the mixture was
stirred at room temperature under argon for 2 minutes. The crude product
was filtered through a short plug of silica gel using dichloromethane (10
mL) as eluent to give the desired cyclic NHC-borane. The title compound
was purified by column chromatography (50% dichloromethane/50% petroleum
ether) to give 2m in 74% yield as a white solid. m.p. 117.0 °C 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 0.70-2.20 (m, 2H), 2.32 (bs, 1H), 2.72 (dd, 1H,
2J = 14.0 Hz, 3J = 9.8 Hz), 3.05 (dd, 1H, 2J = 14.0 Hz, 3J = 6.0 Hz),
3.66 (dd, 1H, 2J = 11.2 Hz, 3J = .1 Hz), 4.02 (dd, 1H, 2J = 11.2 Hz, 3J =
8.3 Hz), 6.98 (d, 1H, 3J = 2.0 Hz), 7.30 (d, 1H, 3J = 2.0 Hz), 7.33-7.39
(m, 3H), 7.46-7.54 (m, 4H), 7.70-7.74 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm) 33.5(HMQC), 42.4, 55.6, 117.2, 120.5, 121.1, 124.9 (q, 3JC-F = 3.7
Hz), 124.6 (q, 1JC-F = 271.0 Hz), 127.3, 127.6, 128.9, 129.6, 138.1,
148.7.11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) -21.9 (t, 1JB-H = 92.6 Hz). HRMS
(ES, [M+Na]+) calcd for [C19H18BF3N2Na]+: 365.1411; found: 365.1410 FT-IR
(ATR) ν (cm-1) 3142 (w), 3053 (w), 2923 (w), 2852 (w), 2349 (w), 2300
(w), 2259 (w), 1611 (w), 1598 (w), 1551 (w), 1507 (w), 144 (w), 1419 (w),
1312 (s), 1266 (w), 1235 (w), 1159 (w), 1115 (w), 1065 (w), 1013 (w), 967
(w), 909 (w), 849 (w), 818 (w), 761 (w), 736 (w), 689 (w). HPLC:
Enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC with a Chiralpak AD-H,
Hexane/isopropanol 95/5, 1 mL/min, UV 254 nm et CD 254nm; rt (minor) =
11.7 min, rt (major)= 12.5 min; 4.3:95.7 er. [α]20 D: -24.1, c = 1,
