$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Hydroboration of Various
Unsaturated Carbonyl Compounds. A dry nitrogen-flushed 50 mL flask
equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and a reflux condenser attached to
a mercury bubbler through a septum inlet was charged with Pt(PPh3)4(56
mg, 0.045 mmol) and bis- (pinacolato)diborane(4) (381 mg, 1.5 mmol). The
carbonyl compound (1.4 mmol) dissolved in 20 mL of toluene was then
added. After the mixture was stirred overnight at 110 °C, the toluene was
removed under vacuum. The mixture was washed with a small amount of cold
water and extracted with pentane. The extracts were dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate. The pentane was removed under vacuum, and the product
was purified by silica gel column chromatography, with 10% ether/
petroleum ether as eluent. 3c: 74%, 0.27 g yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 1.66
(s, 6H, CH3), 1.24 (s, 6H, CH3), 2.81 (m, 2H, CH2, 3JH-H = 5.15, 2JH-H =
11.21, 3JH-H = 18.4 Hz), 3.04 (dd, 1H, CH, 3JH-H = 5.15, 3JH-H = 18.4
Hz), 7.25 (m, 5H, Ph), 9.80 (s, 1H, C=O(H)). 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3): δ 24.46
(CH3), 24.53 (CH3), 47.54 (CH2), 83.64 (CCH3), 125.72 (para CH), 128.42
(ortho or meta CH), 128.57 (ortho or meta CH), 141.18 (ipso), 201.86
(C=O) (CHB cannot be detected). 11B NMR (CDCl3): δ 32.88. Anal. Calcd for
C15H21O3B: C, 69.29; H, 8.16. Found: C, 69.83; H, 7.98. MS (EI): m/z (%)
M+ 260, 245 (M+ - 15, 1.43), 202 (4.96), 177 (6.25), 160 (12.75), 145
(30.89), 132, (56.48), 117 (100), 105 (27.11), 77 (31.50), 84 (49.64) 59
(29.06), 43 (91.38).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Addition Reactions of Bis(pinacolato)diborane(4) to Carbonyl Enones and
Synthesis of (pinacolato)2BCH2B and (pinacolato)2BCH2CH2B by Insertion
and Coupling
