$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: An oven-dried vial was charged with [Cu(CH3
CN)4] PF 6 (7.5 mg, 0.02 mmol, 10.0 mol%) and (R)-DTBM-Segphos (26 mg,
0.022 mmol, 11.0 mol%) and sealed with a septum. The vial was connected
to an argon-vacuum line, evacuated and backfilled with argon (× 3). THF
(1.0 mL/0.2 mmol of 1) was added and the mixture was stirred for 30 min
at room temperature. With the vial still connected to the double line,
the solvent was removed to dryness. Then, a solution of B2pin2 (1.1
equiv) in THF (0.6 mL/0.2 mmol of 1) was added and the mixture was
stirred for 10 min. A 0.2 M NaO'Bu solution in THF (50 μL, 0.1 mmol, 0.5
equiv) was then added dropwise and the dark brown solution was stirred
for 10 min. The reaction mixture was cooled at -78 °C for 10 min and the
corresponding cyclopropene 1 (0.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was added followed by
methanol (32 μL, 0.8 mmol, 4.0 equiv). Then, the reaction mixture was
stirred overnight at the optimized temperature for each case (-20, -50 or
-78 °C). Et2O and water were added and the layers were separated. The
aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O (×3) and the combined organic
layers were washed with saturated NaCl solution, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash-
column chromatography (0-5% Et2O/pentane). From 1a (29 μL, 0.2 mmol),
following the general procedure described above (-20 °C, 12 h),
4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-[(1R,2R)-2-methyl-2-phenylcyclopropyl]-1,3,2-dioxaborolane,
(R,R)-2a. (38.2 mg, 0.15 mmol) was obtained in 74% yield as a colorless
oil.Compound (R,R)-2a was obtained with a 95:5 enantiomeric ratio
determined by SFC using Chiralpak-IC column[CO2 /MeOH (99:1), 1.0
mL/min], diastereomeric ratio: 97:3. [α]20D = -109.4 (c = 1.20, CHCl3).
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.25-7.03 (m, 5H), 1.42 (s, 3H), 1.20 (d, J =
5.1 Hz, 12H), 1.11 (dd, J = 9.7, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 0.98-0.90 (m, 1H), 0.29
(dd, J = 9.7, 7.3 Hz, 1H). τmajor = 6.4 min, τminor = 7.4 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on catalyst, optimized on
solvent, optimized on temperature, sealed vial used, diastereomeric ratio
97:3, er ratio 95:5, optimized on ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
