$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Cu-Catalyzed
β-Borylation of Thioacetylenes. To a mixture of CuCl (5.0 mg, 0.05 mmol),
DPEphos (27.0 mg, 0.05 mmol), NaOt-Bu (7.2 mg, 0.075 mmol), and B2pin2
(2a) (69.9 mg, 0.55 mmol) was added a solution of 1a (81 mg, 0.5 mmol) in
2 mL of MeOH under a nitrogen atmosphere. After stirring at 35 °C for 12
h, the reaction mixture was concentrated and purified by column
chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1) on silica gel to give 3a.
Compound 3i. 73% yield (124 mg); white solid. mp: 98-100 °C; Rf = 0.30
(petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 1.29 (s, 12H),
1.32 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 2.81 (q, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 7.36 (s, 1H),
7.38-7.44 (m, 2H), 7.47-7.52 (m, 1H), 7.76-7.82 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
100 MHz): δ 15.5, 24.7, 28.8, 83.6, 125.4, 125.6, 127.30, 127.34, 127.5,
128.0, 132.2, 133.3, 137.3, 145.6; MS (EI, m/z): 340 (M+, 4), 212 (7),
184 (29), 152 (100); HRMS (EI) calcd for C20H25BO2S (M+) 340.1668, found
340.1668.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (Z)-1-Thio- and (Z)-2-Thio-1-alkenyl Boronates via
Copper-Catalyzed Regiodivergent Hydroboration of Thioacetylenes: An
Experimental and Theoretical Study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
