$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 23. To a solution of dimesitylvinylphosphine (100 mg, 0.34
mmol) and HB(C6F5)2 (117 mg, 0.34 mmol) in pentane (10 mL) norbornene
(621 mg, 6.6 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 8 days
at room temperature, during this time a white solid precipitated. The
precipitate was isolated via cannula filtration and washed with pentane
(10 mL) and dried in vacuo to yield 23 (173 mg). 23, yield 72% Anal.
Calc. for C39H36BF10P: C, 63.60; H, 4.93. Found C, 63.91; H, 5.42. 1H NMR
(600 MHz, 298 K, C6D6/CD2Cl2) δ = 6.65 (1H, br, m-MesA), 6.55 (1H, br,
m’-MesA), 6.55 (1H, br, m-MesB), 6.48 (1H, br, m’-MesB), 3.29 (1H, m,
2-H), 3.20 (1H, m, 3-H), 2.89, 2.63 (each 1H, each m, PCH2), 2.57 (3H, s,
o-CH3MesB), 2.41 (3H, s, o-CH3MesA), 2.21 (1H, dm, 3JPH = 35.5 Hz, BCH2),
2.02 (3H, s, pCH3MesA), 2.00 (1H, br, 1-H), 1.94 (3H, s, pCH3MesB), 1.79
(1H, dd, 3JHH = 12.0 Hz, 3.5 Hz, 4-H), 1.70 (3H, s, o’CH3MesA), 1.60 (3H,
s, o’CH3MesB), 1.42 (2H, m, 6-H), 1.23, 1.11 (each 1H, each m, 5-H),
1.19, 0.72 (each 1H, each m, 7-H), 0.36 (1H, m, BCH2). 13C{1H} NMR (151
MHz, 298 K, C6D6/CD2Cl2) δ = 149.2 (dm, 1JFC = 238 Hz, 2 × C6F5), 148.5
(dm, 1JFC = 234 Hz, 2 × C6F5), 143.9 (d, 2JPC = 8.3 Hz, o-MesB), 143.2
(d, 4JPC = 2.8 Hz, p-MesA), 142.9 (d, 4JPC = 2.8 Hz, p-MesB), 142.7 (d,
2JPC = 8.2 Hz, o-MesA), 141.3 (d, 2JPC = 8.2 Hz, o’-MesA), 141.1 (d, 2JPC
= 9.1 Hz, o’-MesB), 138.1 (dm, 1JFC = 263 Hz, 2 × C6F5), 137.2 (dm, 1JFC=
251 Hz, 4 × C6F5), 132.7 (d, 3JPC = 10.6 Hz, m’-MesB), 132.4 (d, 3JPC =
10.2 Hz, m’-MesA), 132.0 (d, 3JPC = 10.9 Hz, m-MesA), 131.5 (d, 3JPC =
11.0 Hz, m-MesB), 123.0 (d, 1JPC = 72.2 Hz, i-MesA), 122.3 (d, 1JPC =
75.9 Hz, i-MesB), 44.0 (d, 1JPC = 32.9 Hz, C3), 43.7 (C1), 42.8 (C4),
38.3 (C7), 37.6 (br, C2), 33.9 (d, 3JPC = 14.9 Hz, C5), 32.4 (C6), 25.9
(d, 1JPC = 41.5 Hz, PCH2), 24.8 (o-CH3MesB), 24.6 (d, 3JPC = 2.4 Hz,
o-CH3MesA), 22.3 (d, 3JPC = 5.2 Hz, o’CH3MesA), 22.2 (d, 3JPC = 5.1 Hz,
o’CH3MesB), 20.9 (d, 5JPC = 1.4 Hz, pCH3MesA), 20.6 (d, 5JPC = 1.3 Hz,
pCH3MesB), 14.8 (br, BCH2), n. o. (i-C6F5). 11B{1H} NMR (96 MHz, 298 K,
C6D6/CD2Cl2) δ = –11.8 (ν1/2 = 70 Hz). 31P{1H} NMR (122 MHz, 298 K, C6D6/
CD2Cl2) δ = 31.2 (ν1/2 = 15 Hz). 19F{1H} NMR (282 MHz, 298 K, C6D6/
CD2Cl2) δ = –132.1 (br, 4F, o-C6F5), –162.8, –163.8 (each 1F, p-C6F5),
–165.9, –166.5 (each 2F, m-C6F5). 1H, 1H COSY (600 MHz / 600 MHz, 298K,
C6D6/CD2Cl2) δ = 6.65 / 6.55, 2.41, 2.02, 1.70 (m-MesA / m’-MesA,
o-CH3MesA, pCH3MesA, o’CH3MesA), 6.55 / 6.65, 2.41, 2.02, 1.70 (m’-MesA /
m-MesA, o-CH3MesA, pCH3MesA, o’CH3MesA), 6.55 / 6.48, 2.57, 1.94, 1.60
(m-MesB / m’-MesB, o-CH3MesB, pCH3MesB, o’CH3MesB), 6.48 / 6.55, 2.57,
1.94, 1.60 (m’-MesB / m-MesB, o-CH3MesB, pCH3MesB, o’CH3MesB), 3.29 /
3.20 (2-H / 3-H), 3.20 / 3.29, 2.63, 0.72 (3-H / 2-H, PCH2, 7-H), 2.89
