$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1,3-Dimethyl-1H-benzo[d]imidazol-3-ium-2-yl)(3-methylbutan-2-yl)dihydroborate
(13): Iodine (10.0 mg, 0.04 mmol) was added to a solution of
diMe-BenzImd-BH3 (64.0 mg, 0.4 mmol) and 2-methyl-2-butene (30.8 mg, 0.44
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL). The solution was charged to a small vial and
stirred for 1 d. The solvent was evaporated and the crude product was
purified by flash column chromatography. The title compound (65.3 mg,
71%) as viscous colorless oil: 1H NMR (300 MHz, C6D6) δ 6.93 (m, 2H),
6.62 (m, 2H), 3.41 (s, 6H), 2.12 (m, 1H), 1.46 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.44
(d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.17 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.01 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR
(125 MHz, C6D6) δ 184.3 (br), 132.8, 122.9, 110.0, 35.6, 31.4, 22.0,
21.3, 19.5; 11B NMR (160.5 MHz, C6D6) δ -25.3 (t, JB-H = 85 Hz); FTIR
(thin film, CH2Cl2, cm-1) ν = 2944, 2858, 2293, 1464, 1198, 741; HRMS
(ESI) m/z (M+ + H) calculated for C14H24BN2 231.2033, found 231.2035.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, 1.1 eq. of alkene used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Molecular Iodine Initiates Hydroborations of Alkenes with N-Heterocyclic
Carbene Boranes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pan, Xiangcheng; Boussonniere, Anne; Curran, Dennis P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(38), 14433-14437

