$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1,4-Dimethyl-1H-1,2,4-triazol-4-ium-5-yl)(3-methylbutan-2-yl)dihydroborate
(12): Iodine (10.0 mg, 0.04 mmol) was added to a solution of diMe-Tri-BH3
(44.4 mg, 0.4 mmol) and 2-methyl-2-butene (30.8 mg, 0.44 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(0.5 mL). The solution was charged to a small vial and stirred for 1 d.
The solvent was evaporated and the crude product was purified by flash
column chromatography. The title compound (50.7 mg, 70%) as viscous
colorless oil: 1H NMR (500 MHz, C6D6) δ 6.48 (s, 1H), 3.53 (s, 3H), 2.84
(s, 3H), 1.97 (m, 1H), 1.36 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 1.34 (d, J = 6.5 Hz,
3H), 1.06 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.82 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, C6D6) δ
171.8 (br), 140.6, 37.4, 35.3, 32.5, 30.4 (q, JB-C = 36 Hz), 22.0, 21.2,
19.4; 11B NMR (160.5 MHz, C6D6) δ -25.9 (t, JB-H = 88 Hz); FTIR (thin
film, CH2Cl2, cm-1) ν = 2944, 2856, 2277, 1546, 1497, 1458, 1375, 1218,
1048; HRMS (ESI) m/z (M+ + H) calculated for C9H21BN3 182.1829, found
182.1836.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, 1.1 eq. of alkene used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Molecular Iodine Initiates Hydroborations of Alkenes with N-Heterocyclic
Carbene Boranes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
