$DATUM Synthesis of 20. Dimesitylvinylphosphine (100 mg, 0.34 mmol) and
HB(C6F5)2 (117 mg, 0.34 mmol) were dissolved in pentane (10 mL) and
stirred for 15 min. Upon addition of cinnamaldehyde (42 μL, 0.34 mmol) at
room temperature a white precipitate was immediately formed. After
stirring the reaction mixture overnight, the precipitate was isolated via
cannula filtration. Then the residue was washed twice with pentane (2 mL)
and all volatiles were removed in vacuo to yield 20 (184 mg). 20, yield
70% Anal. Calc. for C41H34BF10OP: C, 63.58; H, 4.42. Found C, 63.12; H,
4.54. 1H NMR (600 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ = 7.29 (2H, m, m-Ph), 7.23 (3H,
m, p-, o-Ph), 6.98 (2H, br s, m-MesA), 6.94 (2H, br s, m-MesB), 6.93 (1H,
ddd, 3JHH = 15.5 Hz, 4JPH = 6.2 Hz, 4JHH =1.9 Hz, =CHPh), 6.11 (1H, dt,
3JHH = 15.5 Hz, 3JPH ≈ 3JHH = 4.3 Hz, =CH), 5.74 (1H, ddd, 2JPH = 6.2 Hz,
4JHH = 1.9 Hz, 3JHH = 4.3 Hz, HCO), 3.31, 3.04 (each 1H, each br m,
PCH2), 2.36 (6H, s, o-CH3MesB), 2.32 (3H, s, p-CH3MesA), 2.28 (3H, s,
p-CH3MesB), 2.23 (6H, s, o-CH3MesA), 1.67, 1.02 (each 1H, each br m,
BCH2). 13C{1H} NMR (151 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ = 144.3 (p-MesA), 143.7
(p-MesB), 142.8 (o-MesB), 142.5 (o-MesA), 136.7 (d, 4JPC = 3.8 Hz, i-Ph),
133.8 (d, 3JPC = 12.1 Hz, =CHPh), 132.7 (br d, 3JPC = 7.7 Hz, m-MesA),
131.5 (br d, 3JPC = 7.7 Hz, m-MesB), 129.0 (m-Ph), 128.3 (p-Ph), 126.9
(o-Ph), 123.6 (=CH), 122.8 (d, 1JPC = 60.5 Hz, i-MesB), 119.6 (d, 1JPC =
60.5 Hz, i-MesA), 81.3 (d, 1JPC = 35.1 Hz, HCO), 28.4 (d, 1JPC = 42.1 Hz,
PCH2), 24.5 (o-CH3MesA), 23.6 (o-CH3MesB), 21.1 (pCH3MesA,B), 13.9 (br,
BCH2), n. o. (C6F5). 11B{1H} NMR (192 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ = –0.5 (ν1/2
= 150 Hz). 31P{1H} NMR (243 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ = 16.1 (ν1/2 = 12 Hz).
19F{1H} NMR (564 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ = –134.6 (2F, o-), –162.5 (1F,
p-), –166.4 (2F, m-) (C6F5A), –134.8 (2F, o-), –161.4 (1F, p-), –165.6
(2F, m-) (C6F5B). 1H,1H GCOSY (600 MHz / 600 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ (1H,
1H) = 7.29 / 7.23 (m-Ph / p-, o-Ph), 7.23 / 7.29 (p-, o-Ph / m-Ph), 6.98
/ 2.32, 2.23 (m-MesA / pCH3MesA, o-CH3MesA), 6.94 / 2.36, 2.28 (m-MesB /
o-CH3MesB, pCH3MesB), 6.93 / 6.11, 5.74 (=CHPh / =CH, HCO), 6.11 / 6.93,
5.74 (=CH / =CHPh, HCO), 5.74 / 6.93, 6.11 (HCO / =CHPh, =CH), 3.31, 3.04
/ 1.67, 1.02 (PCH2 / BCH2), 2.36 / 6.94 (o-CH3MesB / m-MesB), 2.32 / 6.98
(pCH3MesA / m-MesA), 2.28 / 6.94 (pCH3MesB / m-MesB), 2.23 / 6.98
(o-CH3MesA / m-MesA), 1.67, 1.02 / 3.31, 3.04 (BCH2 / PCH2). 1H,13C GHSQC
(600 MHz / 151 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ (1H) / δ (13C) = 7.29 / 129.0
(m-Ph), 7.23 / 128.3 (p-Ph), 7.23 / 126.9 (o-Ph), 6.98 / 132.7 (m-MesA),
6.94 / 131.5 (m-MesB), 6.93 / 133.8 (=CHPh), 6.11 / 123.6 (=CH), 5.74 /
81.3 (HCO), 3.31, 3.04 / 28.4 (PCH2), 2.36 / 23.6 (o-CH3MesB), 2.32, 2.28
/ 21.1 (pCH3MesA, pCH3MesB), 2.23 / 24.5 (o-CH3MesA), 1.67, 1.02 / 13.9
(BCH2). 1H,13C GHMBC (600 MHz / 151 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ (1H) / δ (13C)
= 7.29 / 136.7, 129.0, 128.3, 126.9 (m-Ph / i-Ph, m-Ph, p-Ph, o-Ph), 7.23
/ 133.8, 128.3, 126.9 (p-, o-Ph / =CHPh, p-, o-Ph), 6.98 / 132.7, 119.6,
24.5, 21.1 (m-MesA / m-MesA, i-MesA, o-CH3MesA, pCH3MesA), 6.94 / 131.5,
23.6, 21.1 (m-MesB / m-MesB, o-CH3MesB, pCH3MesB), 6.93 / 136.7, 126.9,
123.6, 81.3 (=CHPh, i-Ph, o-Ph, =CH, CH), 6.11 / 136.7, 133.8, 81.3 (=CH
/ i-Ph, =CHPh, HCO), 5.74 / 133.8, 123.6 (HCO / =CHPh, =CH), 2.36 /
142.8, 131.5 (o-CH3MesB / o-MesB, m-MesB), 2.32 / 144.3, 132.7 (pCH3MesA
/ p-MesA, m-MesA), 2.28 / 143.7, 131.5 (pCH3MesB / p-MesB, m-MesB), 2.23
/ 132.7, 142.5 (o-CH3MesA / m-MesA, o-MesA). 19F{1H}, 19F{1H} GCOSY (564
/ 564 MHz, 298 K, CD2Cl2) δ (19F) / δ (19F) = –134.6 /–166.4 (o-C6F5A /
m-C6F5A), –134.8 / –165.6 (o-C6F5B / m-C6F5B), –161.4 / –165.6 (p-C6F5B /
m-C6F5B), –162.5 / –166.4 (p-C6F5A / m-C6F5A), –165.6 / –134.8, –161.4
(m-C6F5B / o-C6F5B, p-C6F5B), –166.4 /–134.6, –162.5 (m-C6F5A / o-C6F5A,
p-C6F5A). m. p. (DSC) = 205 °C. IR (KBr) v~ [cm-1] = 3033 (s), 2954 (vs),
2921 (vs), 2714 (s), 2361 (m), 2311 (w), 1946 (w), 1879 (w), 1825 (w),
1738 (w), 1715 (w), 1643 (vs), 1605 (s), 1558 (m), 1517 (m), 1388 (m),
