$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for hydroboration of 1 a-h:
Pinacolborane (2 eq) was added to the phosphonoalkene neat at room
temperature and reaction mixture was stirred at 70°C for 1h (method A) or
at 110°C for 5h (method B) . The excess of pinacolborane was distilled
under reduced pressure and residue was chromatographed on silica gel
(80:20 chloroform:ethyl acetate). 2g. 1HNMR (CDCl3): δ=0.07(s, 3H), 0.08
(s, 3H), 0.88 (s, 9H), 0.95 (t, 2H), 1.25 ( s, 12H), 1.31 (t, 6H),
1.7-1.9(m, 2H), 3.88 ( m, 1H), 4.05-4.17 (q, 4H).13C (CDCl3): δ=4.69, 8.5
(br), 16.55, 24.64, 25.75, 24.94, 62.14, 670.64 (d, J=234 Hz), 83.10.31P
(CDCl3): δ=24.02. 11BNMR (CDCl3): δ=34.01.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydroboration of Unsaturated Phosphonic Esters: Synthesis of
Boronophosphonates and Trisubstituted Vinylphosphonates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pergament, Inna; Srebnik, Morris
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2001), 3(2), 217-219

