$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(3):CAS_RN
$DATUM 5614-37-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3. General procedure for Scheme 2. Catalysts
and reagents were stored in air. A vial was charged with [Cu(Cl)(IMes)]
(stock solution 0.005 mmol in 3.3 mL of CH2Cl2. The latter was removed in
vacuo before addition of other reagents), NaOH (0.025 mmol, 1 mg),
bis-(pinacolato)diboron (0.55 mmol, 140 mg, 1.1 equiv.), the alkyne (0.5
mmol), CPME (0.6 mL) and MeOH (1.0 mmol, 0.05 mL). The vial was closed
with a screw-cap, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 25 ºC for 16 h.
Conversion was determined by GC analysis. The volatiles were removed in
vacuo and the products were purified by column chromatography (SiO2). The
regioselectivity of the reaction was determined by 1H NMR. 1H and
13C-{1H} NMR data were found similar to literature values for 2a,[3]
3a,[6] 4a,[7] 5a,[3] 7a,[3] 8a,[3] and 9a.[3]
(Z)-4-(4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(1-phenylprop-1-en-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane,
2a [3]
(Z)-trimethyl-(2-phenyl-1-(4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)vinyl)silane,
3a [6] After purification (SiO2, pentane) 3a was isolated as a colorless
solid in 70 % yield (0.105 g). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K): δ = 7.39
(br s, 1H, CH=C-Si), 7.32 -7.31 (m, 4H, CH phenyl), 7.23 -7.18 (m, 1H, CH
phenyl), 1.26 (s, 12H), -0.12 (s, 9H, CH 3-Si).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, regioselective, stereoselective, conversion,
77%, sealed vial used, isomer ratio (>98:2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-Catalyzed Regioselective Formation of Tri- and Tetrasubstituted
Vinylboronates in Air
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bidal, Yannick D.; Lazreg, Faima; Cazin, Catherine S. J.
