$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (26) In a typical experiment, a mixture of B2(cat)2 (52 mg, 0.22 mmol),
phenyl vinyl sulfide (27 mg, 0.20 mmol), and Pt(dba)2 (7 mg, 0.01 mmol)
was dissolved in 0.5 mL of C6D6 and stirred for 2 days to afford 11 (93%)
and 10 (6%), along with minor amounts of B2(cat)3. Reactions were
monitored by multinuclear NMR spectroscopy. NMR for 11: 11, yield (93%),
10, yield (6%). 1H δ 7.4-6.6 (ov m, 13H, Ph and cat), 3.45 (dd, J = 9, 7
Hz, 1H, CH), 1.99 (dd, J = 17, 9 Hz, 2H, CH2), 1.91 (dd, J = 17, 7 Hz,
2H, CH2); 11B{1H} δ 35.1 (br); 13C{1H} NMR: δ 148.5 (C cat), 135.1 (ipso
of Ph), 132.8 (Ph), 129.1 (Ph), 127.5 (Ph), 123.0, 122.8 (CH cat), 112.8,
112.6 (CH cat), 25.9 (br, CH-B), 14.2 ppm (br, CH2-B). NMR: 1H δ 7.25-6.6
(ov m, 9H, Ph and cat), 3.02 (q, J = 8 Hz, 1H, CH), 1.48 (d, J = 8 Hz,
3H, CH3); 11B{1H} δ 33.4 (br); 13C{1H} δ 148.4 (C cat), 131.7, 129.1,
127.0, 123.0 (CH cat), 112.7 (CH cat), 24.0 (br, C-B), 16.7 (CH3).
