$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Cu-Catalyzed
α-Borylation of Thioacetylenes. To a mixture of CuCl (5.0 mg, 0.05 mmol),
Xantphos (28.8 mg, 0.05 mmol), and NaOt-Bu (9.6 mg, 0.1 mmol) in 0.5 mL
of toluene was added neat HBpin (150 μL, 1.0 mmol) under a nitrogen
atmosphere. After stirring at 0 °C for 15 min, 1a (0.5 mmol) was added at
0 °C, followed by stirring at 25 °C for 12 h (determined by GC). The
reaction mixture was concentrated and purified by column chromatography
(petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1) on silica gel to give 4a. Compound 4m. 80%
yield (127 mg); colorless oil. α/β = 96:4; Rf = 0.40 (petroleum
ether/EtOAc = 30:1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ 0.90 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H),
1.07 (s, 12H), 1.33-1.40 (m, 2H), 1.42- 1.48 (m, 2H), 2.44 (q, J = 7.4
Hz, 2H), 6.77 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 7.09- 7.13 (m, 1H), 7.20-7.24 (m, 2H),
7.26-7.29 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 150 MHz): δ 13.9, 22.4, 24.4, 30.4,
30.8, 83.8, 125.4, 128.5, 128.9, 138.0, 152.3; MS (EI, m/z): 318 (M+,
100), 241 (2), 209 (16), 191 (19); HRMS (EI) calcd for C18H27BO2S (M+)
318.1825, found 318.1825.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (Z)-1-Thio- and (Z)-2-Thio-1-alkenyl Boronates via
Copper-Catalyzed Regiodivergent Hydroboration of Thioacetylenes: An
Experimental and Theoretical Study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhu, Gangguo; Kong, Wei; Feng, Hui; Qian, Zhaosheng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(4), 1786-1795

